{
  "_comment": "Cross-language parity for the run-limits registry (run-limits.ts / run_limits.py). 'parse': parseDuration / parse_duration input to milliseconds or \"none\", with the canonical formatDuration / format_duration form, or the exact error sentence. 'settings': ~/.tidegap/config lines to the values kept (by key) and the lines ignored with their reason. 'resolve' and 'legacy': config lines, stored caps and a runner to each effective limit with its source. Consumed by packages/core-ts/test/run-limits.test.ts and packages/core-py/tests/test_run_limits.py.",
  "errors": {
    "form": "Use a duration from 1s to 7d, such as 90s, 30m, 1.5h or 2d, or none for no time limit.",
    "zero": "0 is not a time limit; use none for no time limit.",
    "range": "A time limit must be from 1s to 7d; use none for no time limit."
  },
